lizard bonesnapper~
a bonesnapper~
A large lizard walks upright, sniffing the air.
~
The bonesnapper, raised up on its hind legs, walks convulsively on wide,
clawed feet. Standing about five feet tall, its tough hide is thick and
leathery, like the bark of an ancient tree. Ridges of bone alternate down the
length of its neck and back, ending in two sharp spikes at the tip of a
massive tail. Its dark green color enables it to vanish into the foliage.
~
